{"id":"word:hebrew:H802","type":"word","title":"אִשָּׁה","subtitle":"H802 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a woman","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אִשָּׁה (H802) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 781 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אִשָּׁה (ʼishshâh) means a woman First listed occurrence: 1Chr 1 50."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אִשָּׁה","transliteration":"ʼishshâh","pronunciation":"ish-shaw'","strong":"H802","lemmaId":"hebrew:H802","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["אֵ֣שֶׁת","לְ/אִשָּֽׁה","אִשָּׁ֖ה","אִשָּׁ֥ה","אֵ֥שֶׁת"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",147],["HTd/Ncfsa",103],["HNcfsc",97],["HNcfsc/Sp3ms",66],["HR/Ncfsa",59],["HNcfpa",55],["HTd/Ncfpa",40],["HC/Ncfsa",22],["HR/Ncfpa",17],["HC/Ncfsc/Sp3ms",14]]},"definitions":{"short":"a woman","usage":"(adulter) ess, each, every, female, × many, none, one, together, wife, woman. Often unexpressed in English.","full":"H802. ishshah אִשָּׁה 775 noun feminine woman, wife, female (Arabic , Sabean אנתֿת etc. DHM ZK 1884, 360 , Aramaic אִתָּא אִנְתְּתָא, אִתְּתָא, , , Palmyrene, Nabataean אנתתא , Ethiopic Phoenician אשת , Assyrian aššatu COT Gloss ) — ׳א absolute Genesis 2:33 +; construct אֵשֶׁת Gen 11:29 + (apparently absolute Deut 21:11 ; 1Sam 28:7 ; Psa 58:9 but compare Bö § 728 Ges § 130 . 5); suffix אִשְׁתִּי Gen 20:11 +; אִשְׁתְּךָ 12:18 + ( אֶשְׁתְּךָ Psa 128:3 ), etc.; Plural אִשֹּׁת Ezek 23:44 (Co לעשׂות ); נָשִׁים Gen 4:19 +; construct נְשֵׁי 4:23 +; suffix נָשַׁי 30:26 ; 1Kin 20:7 ; נְשֵׁיכֶם Exod 22:23 +, etc.; — 1 woman Gen 3:1-2 , 12:11 +; opposed to man 2:22-23 , Exod 35:29 ; 36:6 ; Deut 7:2 , 5 ; 22:22 ; 1Sam 21:5 +; ׳א emphatic a Genuine (or ideal) woman Eccl 7:28 (|| אדם ); simile of men as feeble, timid Jer 50:37 ; 51:30 ; note especially בַּנָּשִׁים הַטַּף the children among the women, female children Num 31:18 (P); as conceiving Exod 2:2 ; Lev 12:2 ; 2Sam 11:5 +; travailing Jer 13:21 ; bearing children Judg 13:24 ; 1Kin 3:18 ; compare Job 14:1 ; 15:14 ; 25:4 +, etc.; suckling Isa 49:15 ; כַּנָּשִׁים אֹרַח Gen 18:11 ; נָשִׁים דֶּרֶח 31:35 ; with adjective, or app., מֵינֶקֶת׳א nursing woman, nurse Exod 2:7 ; ׳א זוֺנָה harlot Josh 2:1 ; 6:22 ; Judg 11:1 ; 16:1 ; 1Kin 3:16 ; Prov 6:26 ; Jer 3:3 ; Ezek 16:30 ; 23:44 ; so ׳א זָרָה Prov 2:16 ; 7:5 ; compare also Ezek 23:44 above; ׳א מְנָאָ֑פֶת adulteress Prov 30:20 (compare אִישׁ אֵשֶׁת 6:26 ), זְנוּנִים אֵשֶׁת Hosea 1:2 ; נָכְרִיּוֺת נָשִׁים foreign women 1Kin 11:1 , 8 ; Ezra 10:2 , 10 , 11 , 14 , 17 , 18 , 44 ; Neh 13:26-27 , (compare 13:23 ); ׳א חֲכָמָה wise woman , one known as clever, shrewd 2Sam 14:2 ; 20:16 , etc.; also ׳א מִּילֶגֶשׁ concubine Judg 19:1 , 27: ׳א אַלְמָנָה widow 2Sam 14:5 ; 1Kin 11:26 ; 17:9-10 , ׳א נְבִיאָה prophetess Judg 4:4 ; also construct before noun of quality רָ֑ע אֵשֶׁת Prov 6:24 ; ׳א בְּסִילוּת 9:13 ; ׳א חֵן 11:16 ; ׳א חַיִל 12:4 ; 31:10 ; Ruth 3:11 ; ׳א מִדְיָנִים Prov 21:9 ; 25:24 ; 27:15 ; ׳א ׳מ וָכָ֑עַס 21:19 . 2 Wife (woman belonging to a man, usually construct or suffix) Gen 2:24-25 , 3:8 , 17 ; 4:1 , 17 + often; of one betrothed ( ארשׂ ) Deut 20:7 ; 28:30 ; (הָ)אִשָּׁה בַּעַל Exod 21:3 , 22 ; הָאִשָּׁה אִישׁ Judg 20:4 ; לְאִשָּׁה to wife Gen 2:22 ; 12:19 ; 16:3 ; 34:21 + often (after נָתַן לָקַח, husband or father subject); for wife (after הָֽיְתָה , woman subject) 20:12 ; Num 36:3 , 6 (twice in verse); 36:11-12 , Deut 22:19 , 29 +; for unfaithful wife compare 1 ; construct in phrase חֵיקֶ֑ךָ אֵשֶׁת 13:7 ; compare 28:54 ; ׳א נְעוּרֶיךָ Prov 5:18 ; Mal 2:14-15 , ׳א בְּרִיתֶ֑ךָ 2:14 ; אָב אֵשֶׁת = step-mother Lev 18:8 , 11 ; 20:11 . 3 Female of animals Gen 7:2 (twice in verse); see also below 4 4 With distributive & reciprocal sense, רְעוּתָהּ ׳א מֵאֵת each woman from her neighbour Exod 11:2 (E); compare Ruth 1:8-9 , Jer 9:19 ; each one , of birds of prey Isa 34:15 compare 34:16 (strike out Bi Che); of cows (figurative of heartless women of Israel) Amos 4:3 ; of sheep (figurative of Israel) Zech 11:9 ; & of inanimate things (P, & late) ׳א אֲחֹתָהּ אֶל Exod 26:3 (twice in verse); 26:5-6 , 17 (P) Ezek 1:9 (strike out Co) 1:23 ; 3:13 . אנת (the root of the pronoun 2 person in Shemitic: , anta ; feminine , ant£ ; Biblical Aramaic Kt אַנְתָּה (masculine), אַנְתְּ ᵑ7 & אַתְּ (both masculine & feminine); Syriac , feminine , the n being written but not pronounced; Assyrian atta , feminine atti-e Dl § 55 a, the nt being merged in the double t ; Hebrew similarly. Plural , feminine , Aramaic אַנְתּוּן , , feminine אַתִּין , ; Assyrian attunu ). II. אנשׁ (√ of following; Biblical Hebrew III. אִשָּׁח אנשׁ, ).","rootNote":"feminine of 376 or 582 ; irregular plural, נָשִׁים ;(used in the same wide sense as 582 )","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 50","keyReferences":["1Chr 1 50","1Chr 2 18","1Chr 2 24","1Chr 2 26","1Chr 2 29","1Chr 2 35","1Chr 3 3","1Chr 4 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":781,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 1 50","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":50,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אִשְׁתּ֤/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 18","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אִשָּׁ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אֵ֤שֶׁת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncfsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אִשָּׁ֥ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 29","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֥שֶׁת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 35","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":35,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/אִשָּׁ֑ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 3 3","book":"1Chr","chapter":3,"verse":3,"engl